    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but thats just a bandaid on a bullet wound. like, sure, people are \"healing\" in small ways, but the math doesn't add up. the systems are failing, the environment is collapsing, and it feels like we're just being told to enjoy the view while the ship goes down. it’s hard to find meaning in \"small ways\" when the whole scale of the problem is so massive and certain. it just feels like a slow motion disaster.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
